      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>
We had identified that your house is reasonably air tight and does rely on those 2 x high wall passive air vents in the upper wall of the hallway outside the bedrooms. As the house requires fresh air (primarily when the kitchen range hood fan, a bathroom fan or the clothes dryer is on), outside fresh air is brought in through those 2 vents

Although your house is reasonably air tight, there are a few upgrades that will help to reduce excess air leakage &amp; heat loss:

** The current co-vented chimney &amp; 6" combustion air supply pipe will be eliminated when you install a new high efficiency combi boiler.

** The kitchen range hood fan was not working while I was there, but we did notice (during the blower door test) there was alot of air leakage coming from the wall that it is installed into (so I expect it may not be well installed &amp; sealed)

** The attic access panel allow leakage around the perimeter and can be sealed with a removeable caulking, such as Draft Attack.

** The bathroom fans appear to be worn and allow air leakage. If you choose to replace them with new ENERGY STARÂ® rated units, these will have better spring loaded dampers inside that help prevent excess heat loss.

Savings: There should be a minimum 10% reduction in overall air leakage achieved from completing the above air sealing (especially if the boiler &amp; hot water are upgraded) that could potentially save $ 294 per year in energy costs, decrease your annual energy usage by 8 GJ, and qualify for up to $ 715 in rebates from the Canada Greener Homes Grant initiative. 

CANADA GREENER HOMES GRANT

Through the Canada Greener Homes Grant initiative, a grant of $715 is available for improving the airtightness of your home based on achieving the target outlined above. This grant can increase up to $1,300 based on how much you exceed the target.

An air-sealing grant is available if the airtightness of your home is improved to achieve or exceed the air change rate target proposed above. Achieving any of the targets defined for your home typically requires that the work be performed by an air-sealing professional.</airSeal>
